⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Shudra
node JTI · JTI · ⟦Shudra:JTI:db75dc⟧

WHO   — Shudra — the feet · laborers & servants
WHAT  — The fourth class, tasked with serving the higher three and barred from much religious participation — the feet on which the body stands, ranked lowest within the four (but still inside them).
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the doctrine needed hands to do the work, placed at the bottom of the ranked body — yet, crucially, still within varna, unlike the Dalits.
HOW   — By labor and service, and by exclusion from the rites reserved to the twice-born.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the feet the body stands on — lowest of the four, but inside the body; below me the doctrine put those it would not count at all.

